  "claim": "Marilyn Buck participated in the prison escape of Black Liberation Army member Assata Shakur in 1968.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Marilyn Buck. Sentence: Marilyn Jean Buck (December 13, 1947 – August 3, 2010) was an American Marxist revolutionary, and feminist poet, who was imprisoned for her participation in the 1979 prison escape of Assata Shakur, the 1981 Brink's robbery and the 1983 U.S. Senate bombing.\nPage: Assata Shakur. Sentence: Assata Olugbala Shakur (born JoAnne Deborah Byron; July 16, 1947, often referred to by her married surname Chesimard), is a former member of the Black Liberation Army, a black nationalist urban guerrilla group, who was convicted in 1977 of the first-degree murder, under New Jersey's \"aiding and abetting\" statute, of State Trooper Werner Foerster during a shootout on the New Jersey Turnpike in 1973.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Marilyn Buck. Sentence: Marilyn Jean Buck (December 13, 1947 – August 3, 2010) was an American Marxist revolutionary, and feminist poet, who was imprisoned for her participation in the 1979 prison escape of Assata Shakur, the 1981 Brink's robbery and the 1983 U.S. Senate bombing.\nPage: Assata Shakur. Sentence: Assata Olugbala Shakur (born JoAnne Deborah Byron; July 16, 1947, often referred to by her married surname Chesimard), is a former member of the Black Liberation Army, a black nationalist urban guerrilla group, who was convicted in 1977 of the first-degree murder, under New Jersey's \"aiding and abetting\" statute, of State Trooper Werner Foerster during a shootout on the New Jersey Turnpike in 1973.",
