        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "204ad9dd-886c-56aa-b835-afccffe29ec3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marilyn Buck, Assata Shakur, Werner Foerster\n- Organizations: Black Liberation Army\n- Events: 1973 New Jersey Turnpike shootout, 1979 prison escape of Assata Shakur, 1981 Brink's robbery, 1983 U.S. Senate bombing\n- Roles: Marxist revolutionary, feminist poet, former member\n\nFacts:\n- Assata Shakur was born JoAnne Deborah Byron on July 16, 1947 and is often referred to by her married surname Chesimard.\n- Marilyn Buck was born on December 13, 1947 and was an American Marxist revolutionary and feminist poet.\n- Assata Shakur was involved in a 1973 shootout on the New Jersey Turnpike in which State Trooper Werner Foerster was killed.\n- In 1977, Assata Shakur was convicted under New Jersey's aiding and abetting statute of the first-degree murder of Werner Foerster.\n- Marilyn Buck was imprisoned for participating in the 1979 prison escape of Assata Shakur.\n- Marilyn Buck was also imprisoned for participating in the 1981 Brink's robbery and the 1983 U.S. Senate bombing.\n- Assata Shakur was a former member of the Black Liberation Army, described here as a black nationalist urban guerrilla group.\n- Marilyn Buck died on August 3, 2010.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
